One problem with Lojban is that quantifier scope need not correspond to sen=
tences (in some sense of that word -- certainly not bridi). So the floating=
 'da' is likely picked up already by the earlier quantifier  (the anaphora =
helps this view).  On the other hand, there are no unquantified variables i=
n Lojban, so the sentence never would not make sense, just not the sense wa=
nted.

